    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0441" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg353"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 9th instant, expressing the gratification of the Government
                    of Italy for the presence of two vessels of war of the U. S. Navy at Genoa, on
                    the occasion of the visit of their majesties to the Columbian Exhibition there
                    during September next.</p>
                <p>It has afforded me pleasure to inclose a copy of your note to the Secretary of
                    the Navy.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
